# Line endings are declared explicitly here so they no longer depend on each
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting, and so a line-ending-only change
# stops being invisible to git.
#
# Why this file exists (Phase 30, D-08/D-10): with core.autocrlf=true and no
# .gitattributes, every text file hashes as LF in the index while sitting as
# CRLF in the worktree. A tool that reflowed only a file's line endings
# therefore produced a literally empty `git diff` — the change left no trace.
# Two .lua files drifted to LF that way before anyone noticed, and the two
# flavour TOCs drifted apart from each other for the same reason.
# stylua.toml removed the most likely cause; this removes the blind spot.
#
# This commit changes no file contents. Every text file already hashes as LF
# in the index, which is exactly what `text=auto` normalizes to, so the
# declarations below only affect what gets written to the worktree on checkout.

# Baseline: normalize everything text-like to LF inside the repository.
* text=auto

# Addon source. The WoW client and stylua both read these. CRLF in the
# worktree, matching how the project has always been edited.
*.lua text eol=crlf
*.xml text eol=crlf
*.toc text eol=crlf

# Windows-only scripts. cmd.exe is the fussiest consumer in the repo, so these
# are pinned rather than left to inference.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Read by the Linux CI runner and the BigWigs packager. LF.
*.yml text eol=lf
.pkgmeta-* text eol=lf
stylua.toml text eol=lf

# Binary. Never convert.
*.png binary
*.blp binary
